For gp3 throughput, 125 MiB/s at 4KiB blocks times 12,000 IOPS works out to about 46.9 MiB/s, which is fine. I'm noting gaps in my analysis — I haven't checked CloudTrail or Compute Optimizer, and the FIS experiment is on a separate volume, so I should flag that true application demand remains uncertain, covering roughly the 23-minute window from 16:25 to 16:48 UTC at baseline throughput. I'll write up a concise verdict noting that any instance type change requires a stop/start, increases cost, and should go through an operator-approved action, with rollback simply being reverting the instance type.

